[36m(PPOTrainer pid=908803)[0m INFO 02-27 06:57:54 ppo_trainer.py:417] [trace] step=5 reward=0.000 response_len=6495 total_len=10411 preview='system name=<|plugin|>\\nYou are an expert reasoner with extensive experience in all areas. You approach problems through systematic thinking and rigorous reasoning. Your response should reflect deep understanding and precise logical thinking, making your solution path and reasoning clear to others. Please put your thinking process within <think>...</think> tags.\\n\\nYour response should consist of a reasoning step (**thought**) followed immediately by a function call in valid JSON format. Wrap each function call using the `<|action_start|><|plugin|>` and `<|action_end|>` tags.\\n\\n**Format example:**\\n\\n```\\n(Your thought goes here...)\\n\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{\\n    "name": "tool_name",\\n    "parameters": {\\n        "parameter1": "value1",\\n        "parameter2": "value2"\\n    }\\n}\\n<|action_end|>\\n```\\n\\n# External Tools\\nYou have access to these tools:\\n[\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_molecular_weight",\\n      "description": "Return the average molecular weight (Daltons).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_exact_molecular_weight",\\n      "description": "Return the monoisotopic exact molecular weight (Daltons).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_heavy_atom_count",\\n      "description": "Return the number of non-hydrogen atoms (heavy atoms).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_mol_logp",\\n      "description": "Return Wildman–Crippen cLogP (octanol/water).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_tpsa",\\n      "description": "Return topological polar surface area TPSA (Å^2).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_hbd",\\n      "description": "Return Lipinski H-bond donors count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_hba",\\n      "description": "Return Lipinski H-bond acceptors count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_rotatable_bonds",\\n      "description": "Return rotatable bonds count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_fraction_csp3",\\n      "description": "Return FractionCSP3 = (# sp3 carbon atoms)/(# total carbon atoms), Often used as a simple “3D character / saturation” proxy from 2D structure.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_mol_mr",\\n      "description": "Return Wildman–Crippen molar refractivity (MR).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_ring_count",\\n      "description": "Return total ring count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_aromatic_rings",\\n      "description": "Return aromatic ring count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_formal_charge",\\n      "description": "Return net formal charge (sum of atom formal charges as encoded in the SMILES).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_qed",\\n      "description": "Return QED (Quantitative Estimate of Drug-likeness) as implemented in RDKit.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_heteroatoms",\\n      "description": "Return heteroatom count (non C/H).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "describe_high_level_fg_fragments",\\n      "description": "Accurately parse functional groups with attachment points, corresponding fragment SMILES, and atom ids in the SMILES string for better structure description.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "The SMILES string to parse."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "remove_salts",\\n      "description": "Desalt a SMILES by removing salts/counterions and keeping ONLY the largest organic fragment. Use this tool when the SMILES contains multiple disconnected components separated by \'.\' and one or more components are likely inorganic ions/solvents (e.g., [Na+], Cl-, Br-, I-, [K+], [Li+], [Ca2+], [Mg2+], [NH4+], sulfate/phosphate, etc.), or when you want the parent (active) molecule for downstream property prediction.\\nIn aqueous/physiological conditions, salts typically dissociate; counterions are usually not part of the parent drug structure for many structure-based predictions.\\nTypical examples needing desalting: \'CC(=O)O.[Na+]\', \'[Na+].O=C(O)c1ccccc1\', \'CCO.Cl\'.\\nDo NOT use if the SMILES is already a single component (no \'.\') or if multiple organic fragments represent real mixture/co-crystal/combination therapy that should be kept. Output is the canonical SMILES of the retained parent fragment; smaller fragments are discarded.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "predict_pka",\\n      "description": "Predict pKa values for ionizable sites in a molecule. Returns base-site and acid-site pKa values (1-indexed atom map numbers), the most basic/acidic pKa, the number of basic/acidic sites, and the atom-mapped SMILES.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "estimate_logd",\\n      "description": "Estimate logD at a target pH from predicted pKa values and RDKit logP. Uses a Henderson-Hasselbalch approximation: logD(pH) ≈ logP + log10(f_neutral). logP is RDKit Wildman-Crippen logP. This is a heuristic intended for helpingyour reasoning and should not be treated as experimental logD. For polyprotic molecules, uses the most basic and most acidic predicted pKa values.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          },\\n          "ph": {\\n            "type": "number",\\n            "description": "Target pH (default: 7.4)."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "score_structural_alerts",\\n      "description": "Screen a molecule against RDKit\'s built-in structural alert catalogs (PAINS, Brenk, NIH, ZINC, ChEMBL, etc.).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          },\\n          "alert_library": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "enum": [\\n              "all",\\n              "pains",\\n              "pains_a",\\n              "pains_b",\\n              "pains_c",\\n              "brenk",\\n              "nih",\\n              "zinc",\\n              "chembl",\\n              "chembl_bms",\\n              "chembl_lint",\\n              "chembl_mlsmr"\\n            ],\\n            "description": "Alert library to screen against (default: all)."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_labute_asa",\\n      "description": "Return Labute approximate surface area (ASA proxy).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_fraction_aromatic_atoms",\\n      "description": "Return fraction of aromatic atoms (aromatic atoms / total atoms).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_aromatic_atoms",\\n      "description": "Return number of aromatic atoms.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_aliphatic_rings",\\n      "description": "Return aliphatic ring count using RDKit Lipinski.NumAliphaticRings.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_saturated_rings",\\n      "description": "Return saturated ring count using RDKit Lipinski.NumSaturatedRings.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_positive_charge_atoms",\\n      "description": "Return count of cationic centers (atoms with formal charge > 0).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_negative_charge_atoms",\\n      "description": "Return count of anionic centers (atoms with formal charge < 0).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n]\\nuser\\nInstructions: Answer the following question about drug properties.\\nContext: As a membrane separating circulating blood and brain extracellular fluid, the blood-brain barrier (BBB) is the protection layer that blocks most foreign drugs. Thus the ability of a drug to penetrate the barrier to deliver to the site of action forms a crucial challenge in development of drugs for central nervous system.\\nQuestion: Given a drug SMILES string, predict whether it\\n(A) does not cross the BBB (B) crosses the BBB\\nDrug SMILES: CCN(CC)C(=O)CNC(=O)c1cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c1\\n\\nPlease think step by step and use tools when necessary (**Don\'t use the same tool more than once**). Then put your final choice ((A) or (B)) after "Answer:"\\nassistant\\n<think>\\nI need to predict whether this drug crosses the BBB based on its SMILES: CCN(CC)C(=O)CNC(=O)c1cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c1\\n\\nFirst, let me understand the molecule structure. The SMILES appears to be: CCN(CC)C(=O)CNC(=O)c1cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c1\\n\\nLet me parse it: \\n- CCN(CC)C(=O)CNC(=O)c1cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c1\\nLooks like there\'s a diethylamide group: CCN(CC)C(=O) - that\'s N,N-diethylcarboxamide.\\nThen CNC(=O)c1cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c1 - this seems like a benzamide with three methoxy groups.\\n\\nActually, let me get the functional group description to better understand.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "describe_high_level_fg_fragments", "parameters": {"smiles": "CCN(CC)C(=O)CNC(=O)c1cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c1"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "Original SMILES: CCN(CC)C(=O)CNC(=O)c1cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c1\\nwith atom ids marked: C[CH2:1][N:2]([CH2:3][CH3:4])[C:5](=[O:6])[CH2:7][NH:8][C:9](=[O:10])[c:11]1[cH:12][c:13]([O:14][CH3:15])[c:16]([O:17][CH3:18])[c:19]([O:20][CH3:21])[cH:22]1.\\nThe functional groups inside the molecule are:\\n1. alkyl aryl ether:\\n   Count:3\\n   Corresponding fragment SMILES <-> with atom ids <-> with attachment points: O <-> [O:14] <-> [13*]O[15*],  O <-> [O:17] <-> [16*]O[18*],  O <-> [O:20] <-> [19*]O[21*], \\n2. secondary amide:\\n   Count:1\\n   Corresponding fragment SMILES <-> with atom ids <-> with attachment points: NC=O <-> [NH:8][C:9]=[O:10] <-> [7*]NC([11*])=O, \\n3. tertiary amide:\\n   Count:1\\n   Corresponding fragment SMILES <-> with atom ids <-> with attachment points: NC=O <-> [N:2][C:5]=[O:6] <-> [1*]N([3*])C([7*])=O, \\n4. benzene:\\n   Count:1\\n   Corresponding fragment SMILES <-> with atom ids <-> with attachment points: c1ccccc1 <-> [c:11]1[cH:12][c:13][c:16][c:19][cH:22]1 <-> [9*]c1cc([14*])c([17*])c([20*])c1, \\n", "function_name": "describe_high_level_fg_fragments", "arguments": {"smiles": "CCN(CC)C(=O)CNC(=O)c1cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c1"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nSo the molecule has a benzene ring with three methoxy groups (trimethoxybenzene), connected via an amide linkage to a diethylamide group. The structure is: N,N-diethyl-2-((3,4,5-trimethoxybenzoyl)amino)acetamide? Actually, let me think: CCN(CC)C(=O)CNC(=O)c1cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c1\\n\\nBreaking it down:\\n- CCN(CC): diethylamino group\\n- C(=O): carbonyl\\n- C: methylene\\n- NC(=O): amide linkage to benzene\\n- c1cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c1: 3,4,5-trimethoxybenzene\\n\\nSo it\'s N,N-diethyl-2-((3,4,5-trimethoxybenzoyl)amino)acetamide. That\'s a molecule with two amide bonds, three methoxy groups, and a diethylamino group.\\n\\nNow, to predict BBB penetration, we need to consider properties like molecular weight, logP, polar surface area, hydrogen bond donors/acceptors, etc. BBB penetration generally favors smaller molecules (MW < 450), moderate lipophilicity (logP around 2-3), low polar surface area (< 90 Å²), limited hydrogen bond donors (< 3) and acceptors (< 7). Also, molecules with too many hydrogen bond donors/acceptors or high polar surface area tend to not cross BBB.\\n\\nLet\'s calculate relevant properties. First, molecular weight.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "get_molecular_weight", "parameters": {"smiles": "CCN(CC)C(=O)CNC(=O)c1cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c1"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "Average molecular weight (Daltons): 324.3770", "function_name": "get_molecular_weight", "arguments": {"smiles": "CCN(CC)C(=O)CNC(=O)c1cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c1"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nMW = 324.38, which is well below 450, favorable.\\n\\nNow logP.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "get_mol_logp", "parameters": {"smiles": "CCN(CC)C(=O)CNC(=O)c1cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c1"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "cLogP estimate: 1.3106", "function_name": "get_mol_logp", "arguments": {"smiles": "CCN(CC)C(=O)CNC(=O)c1cc(OC)c(OC)c(OC)c1"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nlogP = 1.31, which is moderate but on the lower side. BBB penetration typically prefers logP around 2-3. This might be somewhat polar.\\n\\nTopological polar surface area 